ution":37.2,"_gate_insider_own":0.0039399997,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":2.6,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"NXP Semiconductors N.V. provides semiconductor products in the United States, Germany, Japan, South Korea, Taiwan, Singapore, the Netherlands, Mainland China, Hong Kong, and internationally. The company's product portfolio includes microcontrollers; application processors; communication processors; wireless connectivity solutions, such as near field communications, ultra-wideband, Bluetooth low-energy, Zigbee, Thread, and Wi-Fi and Wi-Fi/Bluetooth integrated SoCs; analog and interface products; radio frequency devices, and security controllers, as well as semiconductor-based environmental and inertial sensors, including pressure, inertial, magnetic, and gyroscopic sensors. Its products are used in various applications, including automotive, industrial and Internet of Things, mobile, and communication infrastructure. The company markets its products to direct sales offices and independent distributors. NXP Semiconductors N.V. has a strategic partnership with Volkswagen AG to advance automotive semiconductor technology. The company was incorporated in 2006 and is headquartered in Eindhoven, the Netherlands.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Rafael  Sotomayor | CEO, President & Executive Director | Age 56 | Compensation: $1.4M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 32K people. Revenue per employee of $381K ranks in the above the sector median among Technology peers, with revenue growing 8%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $75K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $14K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 4\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (2/10).","financial_summary":["NXP Semiconductors N.V. is a large-cap technology business with a $63.8B market cap on $12.3B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -2% over the past three years and +7% annually across the full decade, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at 17% against a 10% cost of capital, a 7-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it. Gross margins of 52% confirm genuine pricing power.","The business throws off $2.4B in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 20 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.40\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 2.3\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and interest coverage runs at 6.5\u00d7.","Shareholder yield of 3.0% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 3/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Price sits 21% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.2076789286996179},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Insiders are overwhelmingly selling (100% sell ratio) \u2014 the people who know the business want less of it","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","ratio":0.0},{"text":"Revenue growth lags most Technology peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Financial quality metrics lag Technology peers","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Significant goodwill (39% of assets) from past acquisitions \u2014 a soft asset a conservative appraisal discounts to zero","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Technology sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 9% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Cybersecurity liability and talent cost inflation \u2014 a single breach can erase years of goodwill, and the war for engineering talent compresses margins even at scale.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 18% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"ETFs Are Net Sellers of NXP Semiconductors (NXPI) on Nov. 25","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/etfs-net-sellers-nxp-semiconductors-110204408.html","date":"2026-11-27","timestamp":1795777324.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"NXP (NXPI) Down 3.5% Since Last Earnings Report: Can It Rebound?","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3035987/nxp-nxpi-down-3-5-since-last-earnings-report-can-it-rebound?cid=CS-ZC-FT-realtime_blog-3035987","date":"2026-11-26","timestamp":1795707015.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Can NXP Semiconductors (NASDAQ:NXPI) Sustain Its Operating Momentum?","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/stocks/technology/can-nxp-semiconductors-nasdaqnxpi-sustain-its-operating-momentum","date":"2026-11-25","timestamp":1795642920.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Why Is NXP (NXPI) Stock Down Today? Chip Sector Selloff Drags Shares","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/why-nxp-nxpi-stock-down-203113766.html","date":"2026-